 "intro": "Before Arretium in Etruria, 284 BC. The Senones, a Gallic people from the Adriatic coast, are besieging Rome’s ally. You are the praetor Lucius Caecilius Metellus Denter, marching to relieve the town. The sources are brief.",
 "debrief": "Polybius says the Gauls besieged Arretium, the Romans came to help and were defeated, and the praetor Lucius Caecilius was killed. Other writers add that Roman envoys had been murdered by the Senones, and that 13,000 Romans and seven military tribunes died. Rome answered by invading the Senones’ homeland, driving them out and founding the colony of Sena Gallica. The course of the battle is not recorded; the moves here are a reconstruction, and the other choices are what-ifs.",
